Package: fabricctl
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: fabric <archdukejim@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/archdukejim/fabric
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-yaml, python3-jinja2, openssl, curl, ca-certificates, iptables, ufw, dnsutils
Recommends: python3-pykcs11, python3-pykmip
Suggests: docker-ce, ykcs11, opensc-pkcs11, pcscd, softhsm2
Description: install, secure and run a small network fabric
 fabricctl sets up and manages fabric on this host: authoritative DNS
 (BIND9) with RFC2136/TSIG, an internal PKI (Step-CA), 389 Directory
 Server, Keycloak SSO and a management web UI behind client certificates
 and OIDC — every service in a hardened container under systemd
 (fabric.target). Installing the package changes nothing; run
 `sudo fabricctl setup` to install fabric.
